1
00:00:01,210 --> 00:00:03,960
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:34,590 --> 00:01:36,890
[HANA] Here. Food and clothes.

3
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:39,560
You can't be dressed like that.

4
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,140
These'll help you blend in.

5
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,060
[YURU] Hmm.

6
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:48,900
Is this some kind of tunic?

7
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:50,650
[HANA] Uh, yeah, sure.

8
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:52,490
And think of this as a hakama.

9
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:53,910
[DERA] Here, these too.

10
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,870
You'll need something
for your feet.

11
00:01:56,780 --> 00:02:00,450
[HANA] Oh, the small time
Yakuza look suits you.

12
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:01,910
[YURU] And what are these?

13
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,290
Oh, come on.
Surely you've had onigiri.

14
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:07,800
[YURU] A hundred percent rice?
No millet?

15
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,210
There's even seaweed?

16
00:02:09,250 --> 00:02:11,970
Are you showing me
the luxuries of this world?

17
00:02:12,010 --> 00:02:15,510
[sighs] Yeah, I guess those
would be luxuries to you.

18
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:18,140
And how am I meant
to open this container?

19
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,260
Uh?

20
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:24,270
♪

21
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:32,610
There.

22
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:39,910
[Yuru exclaims]

23
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:42,200
[Yuru screams] Whoa!

24
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:44,250
How is it so delicious?

25
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:45,920
Did the gods give you this?

26
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,920
So, you really like it? Here!

27
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,790
-You should have some more!
-[Yuru moans]

28
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,340
Why are you acting
like his grandma?

29
00:02:54,470 --> 00:02:56,680
I wish Asa could eat this
with me.

30
00:02:58,050 --> 00:02:59,470
She'd love it.

31
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,270
-[RIGHT] Oy, Dera.
-[DERA] Hm?

32
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:05,440
What is this place?

33
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:08,730
[DERA] Oh, uh,
we call these things rest stops.

34
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:10,940
It's like a modern day
relay station.

35
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:13,230
They've got food
and latrines inside.

36
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:14,900
Could even get a souvenir,

37
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,450
-if it suits you.
-[BOTH] Uh?

38
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:18,450
[both grunt]

39
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:21,780
You wanna see? We can.

40
00:03:21,830 --> 00:03:23,750
Nay, Dera.

41
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:25,500
We stay beside our master.

42
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:26,710
Why don't you two
have a meal

43
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:28,500
and handle your bodily
essentials?

44
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:31,460
We will see to it that
Yuru comes to no harm.

45
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:34,920
In that case,
don't mind if we do.

46
00:03:34,970 --> 00:03:37,510
-What you think? Ready to eat?
-[HANA] Hm.

47
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:40,430
Hey. No touching
the wheel, got it?

48
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,930
What of the horses?

49
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:43,970
Do they not need to be fed?

50
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:46,190
No worries. I fed them earlier.

51
00:03:52,610 --> 00:03:53,940
♪

52
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,400
[HANA] So, how much
did you tell him?

53
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,700
Well, when I told him

54
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,570
the girl in the keep
wasn't his real sister,

55
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:01,570
he didn't take it well,

56
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:03,370
so I thought
I'd leave it there for now.

57
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:06,410
Didn't wanna throw more at him
than he could handle at once.

58
00:04:06,450 --> 00:04:08,250
You're too nice sometimes.

59
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:09,460
You gotta remember,

60
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,170
-he's still just a kid.
-[sighs]

61
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:14,340
Whatever, I hate children,
so I wouldn't know.

62
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,050
Appreciate you buying me
some grub.

63
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,590
So, where are we
bringing the boy?

64
00:04:19,630 --> 00:04:22,600
You gonna make the poor kid
hang out with you at su casa?

65
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,560
Nah, I compromised my name
and face

66
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,020
during that rescue mission.

67
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:28,640
I'll need a new pad.
I'm ditching that one.

68
00:04:28,690 --> 00:04:31,860
You're homeless and looking
after someone else's kid.

69
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,150
Your life sounds rough.

70
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:34,940
[Dera grunts, sighs]

71
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,900
This is your life too,
I'm afraid.

72
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,690
As a Higashi Village retainer,

73
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:40,530
you'll be expected to help me
deal with this.

74
00:04:40,570 --> 00:04:41,700
Sure.

75
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:44,320
You know I'll do what I can,
but you know...

76
00:04:44,370 --> 00:04:48,120
Great. Then let's get married,
'kay?

77
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:52,880
[HANA] Got your wedding rings
right here!

78
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,960
Good grief.

79
00:04:54,130 --> 00:04:55,840
Are those in your pocket
everywhere you go?

80
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,420
[HANA] You got
another thing comin'

81
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:59,130
if you think
I'd ever marry you!

82
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:02,010
[Dera shushes]
I don't mean a real marriage!

83
00:05:02,050 --> 00:05:03,890
But look, if we wanna
protect Yuru,

84
00:05:03,930 --> 00:05:06,350
we're gonna have to find ways
to blend into the crowd.

85
00:05:06,390 --> 00:05:07,600
Rumors about outsiders

86
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,390
spread like wildfire
in the countryside,

87
00:05:09,430 --> 00:05:12,020
so we'll have to stay
in a populated city.

88
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:14,110
I just don't know
if I can protect him

89
00:05:14,150 --> 00:05:15,610
from so many threats alone!

90
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:18,240
We don't need to get married
for me to help keep him safe!

91
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,530
Why can't we be roommates?

92
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:21,950
Landlords are looking more
to rent to families.

93
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:24,620
It just sounds a bit more stable
than roommates, I guess.

94
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,870
Yeah, okay!
Then how about I'm his sister,

95
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,200
and we justify
the age difference

96
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:30,200
by saying you had me
as a teenager?

97
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:31,620
You could be
a cool single father

98
00:05:31,670 --> 00:05:32,920
who's just trying his best!

99
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:34,460
[DERA] And in this scene,

100
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:36,960
did my wife just dump me
and leave me with the kids?

101
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
[WOMAN 1] I heard his wife ran.

102
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:40,010
[WOMAN 2] Oh, man.
Do you think he cheated?

103
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:41,090
He seems scary.

104
00:05:41,130 --> 00:05:42,800
[DERA] Oh! Maybe I'm a hero,

105
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:44,590
putting on a brave face
for the children

106
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,350
after his wife
tragically passed.

107
00:05:46,390 --> 00:05:47,760
[WOMAN 3] Such a sad story.

108
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:49,220
[WOMAN 4] I can't even imagine.

109
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:51,190
Let's check in and see
if he needs any help.

110
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:53,230
Either way, I'm gonna get
more attention

111
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:55,020
than I can handle
on a mission like this.

112
00:05:55,060 --> 00:05:56,230
Think of the rumors!

113
00:05:56,270 --> 00:05:58,270
So Yuru's from my first wife,

114
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,730
and then I remarried younger.

115
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:01,320
A May-December thing.

116
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,360
There! Glad it's settled.

117
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,780
Thanks for understanding.

118
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:06,620
[HANA] I haven't agreed
to nothin'.

119
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,330
So which one of us should take
the other one's last name?

120
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:12,410
-What do you think?
-[Hana grunts angrily]

121
00:06:12,450 --> 00:06:13,620
[HANA] This sucks!

122
00:06:13,670 --> 00:06:15,790
My heart only belongs
to one man,

123
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:19,710
and that's Jason Statham!
[echoes]

124
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:21,880
[Right grunts]

125
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,760
[RIGHT]
Where do they keep the horses

126
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,300
inside this tiny box?

127
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:28,680
Modern craft has come far
in the past 400 years.

128
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:31,180
Oh, no! Please, forgive
my impudence.

129
00:06:31,890 --> 00:06:33,940
I just realized
I ate all the food myself

130
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:35,600
and didn't remember
to save any for you.

131
00:06:36,150 --> 00:06:38,770
Our master has the kindest
of hearts, does he not?

132
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:40,270
Pay us no mind.

133
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:42,900
We do not require
human sustenance.

134
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,370
[YURU] So, uh,
if it's all right to ask,

135
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,910
what should I call you?

136
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:49,200
[RIGHT] It's up to you.

137
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:51,580
You may even give us new names.

138
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,950
[YURU] Hmm.

139
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:56,500
So perhaps, Lord Right.
And I guess Lady Left?

140
00:06:57,290 --> 00:06:58,920
That sounds so uptight!

141
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,550
Don't concern yourself
with such formality.

142
00:07:01,590 --> 00:07:03,300
We're your daemons after all.

143
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:06,130
Understood. [grunts]

144
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:08,180
-Right.
-[Right chuckles]

145
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,600
[YURU] Left.

146
00:07:10,470 --> 00:07:12,140
Let's not mince words.

147
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:14,020
I want you to tell me
everything you know

148
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:15,140
about me and my sister.

149
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:16,640
[LEFT AND RIGHT] Hm?

150
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:18,230
♪

151
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,940
[RIGHT] Don't get your hopes up.

152
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:25,360
We sat unmoving in the village
for some 400 years.

153
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:27,360
Our knowledge
of the goings-on outside

154
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:29,070
is no more greater than yours.

155
00:07:29,530 --> 00:07:32,290
We only saw the people
who came and went.

156
00:07:32,330 --> 00:07:33,580
We don't even know much

157
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,870
of what happened
inside the village.

158
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:39,750
At one point, locals spoke
of how twins had been born.

159
00:07:39,790 --> 00:07:42,170
We started seeing
our future master

160
00:07:42,210 --> 00:07:43,550
shortly thereafter.

161
00:07:45,630 --> 00:07:47,130
When you were
little more than a pup,

162
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:48,930
I recall your father
would oft take you

163
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:51,050
deep into the mountains
to go hunting.

164
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:52,140
Yeah.

165
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:54,390
The very first memories
I have are of him

166
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:56,230
teaching me about hunting.

167
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:57,640
Back in those days, though,

168
00:07:57,690 --> 00:08:00,360
we saw neither hide
nor hair of your sister.

169
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,320
We feared the worst.

170
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:04,780
That perhaps she had been
taken by an illness

171
00:08:04,820 --> 00:08:07,490
not long after she was
brought unto this world.

172
00:08:08,030 --> 00:08:09,950
Until ten years ago...

173
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:14,620
♪

174
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,920
[LEFT] In the dead of night,

175
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,920
we saw your parents
flee the village

176
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,930
with a young girl in tow.

177
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:30,930
She seemed small for her age

178
00:08:30,970 --> 00:08:33,640
and her blood smelled as yours.

179
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:39,270
And that once little girl
grew up much bigger

180
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,360
and laid waste to our village.

181
00:08:42,110 --> 00:08:44,980
All these years, I thought
our parents left me and Asa

182
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:47,240
with no one to care for us
but each other.

183
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,320
[vehicle passing]

184
00:08:50,820 --> 00:08:53,160
[YURU] But I was the only one
they left.

185
00:09:00,460 --> 00:09:01,540
[Yuru grunts]

186
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,790
Well, all right then.

187
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,750
I'll find this supposed
"real" Asa.

188
00:09:05,790 --> 00:09:07,340
I want to talk to our parents,

189
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,510
and she maybe knows
where they are.

190
00:09:10,510 --> 00:09:11,720
Yeah.

191
00:09:12,130 --> 00:09:13,260
Yeah!

192
00:09:14,010 --> 00:09:15,430
Thanks for waiting.

193
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:18,430
What's wrong?

194
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:20,270
Is something bothering you,
Hana?

195
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:24,400
Because reasons, we're gonna be
your guardians going forward.

196
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,900
Isn't that grand?

197
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,440
Guardians?

198
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:29,400
We're responsible
if you ever get in trouble,

199
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:31,400
-so don't get in trouble!
-By the way,

200
00:09:31,450 --> 00:09:33,570
we're probably gonna be
on the road for a while.

201
00:09:33,610 --> 00:09:35,700
Need to use the latrine
before we go?

202
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,700
[YURU] No. I went over there.

203
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:39,500
[HANA] He's already
getting in trouble!

204
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:41,410
Also, you're gonna
draw attention

205
00:09:41,460 --> 00:09:42,580
sitting there like a punk.

206
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:44,210
Get off of the car.

207
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,500
[YURU] I didn't realize.

208
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:46,750
Is it not a problem

209
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:48,250
that Right and Left
are up there, too?

210
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:51,260
Daemons are invisible to
the majority of normal humans.

211
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:52,670
But we can see them fine?

212
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,630
Those with daemons
of their own to wield

213
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:56,600
are given the ability to see us.

214
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:58,010
We may also show ourselves

215
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,930
to individuals
of our own volition,

216
00:09:59,970 --> 00:10:01,980
should the situation warrant it.

217
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:03,060
Furthermore,

218
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,690
there are some who simply have
the instinct to see us.

219
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:07,400
-[dog barks]
-[WOMAN] Huh?

220
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,820
What's gotten into you?

221
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:11,190
What does he think
he's barking at?

222
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:18,830
[YURU] The Kagemori clan,
was it?

223
00:10:19,450 --> 00:10:21,540
Do they have daemons
of their own?

224
00:10:21,790 --> 00:10:24,460
They do.
A few of them are wielders.

225
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:26,170
And how would you
describe them?

226
00:10:26,210 --> 00:10:27,920
Like a huge pain in the ass.

227
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:30,000
They used to ally with us.

228
00:10:30,050 --> 00:10:31,880
Now, they only live down here.

229
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,720
You can think of them
like a branch family

230
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,340
to Higashi Village.

231
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:37,350
They had some
ideological differences

232
00:10:37,390 --> 00:10:39,430
they just weren't able
to get past.

233
00:10:39,470 --> 00:10:41,720
You don't wanna get involved
with guys like that

234
00:10:41,770 --> 00:10:42,810
if you don't have to.

235
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:45,060
We've got a whole bunch
of names of people we trust

236
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:46,900
written down
in our database.

237
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:49,860
Er, our list of people
with ties to the village.

238
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,360
For a while now,
we've heard rumors

239
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,860
from former village residents

240
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:56,070
that one of the twins was
in league with the Kagemoris.

241
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:59,080
Turns out they weren't
just rumors.

242
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:11,710
[panting]

243
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:18,640
[whimpering]

244
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:21,760
[footsteps]

245
00:11:37,610 --> 00:11:39,530
-[AOI] Come on.
-[elevator dings]

246
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:46,120
Hurry up. Just close the door.

247
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,960
[whimpers]

248
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:56,670
Hey, baby.
Why you running from me?

249
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:59,640
[whimpers] No! Please,
would you just leave me alone?

250
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:02,300
You know we're long past that.

251
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:06,640
If I left you alone,
how would I ever kill you?

252
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,650
[AOI] Stay back.

253
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:13,690
-I'm warning you!
-[chuckles]

254
00:12:14,230 --> 00:12:15,900
You'd better back up,

255
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,610
'cause if you get closer...

256
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,110
[STALKER] Huh?

257
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:23,530
[in demonic voice]
...then you...

258
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:27,000
-[stalker whimpers]
-...will be in my reach.

259
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:31,500
[Aoi chuckles]

260
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:33,840
-[monster growling]
-[stalker whimpers]

261
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:36,090
[JIN] Good evening, Miss Aoi.

262
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:37,380
This is Jin.

263
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:39,590
Regarding your stalker,

264
00:12:39,630 --> 00:12:41,260
consider it handled.

265
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:45,390
[demonic voices moaning]

266
00:12:46,060 --> 00:12:48,350
[JIN] He's never gonna come
near you again.

267
00:12:48,390 --> 00:12:50,190
That much I can promise.

268
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:54,070
You're safe to return
to the office now.

269
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:58,990
On that note,
I'll notify your boss, too.

270
00:13:01,070 --> 00:13:02,530
Pleasure working with you.

271
00:13:02,570 --> 00:13:04,080
[monster growls]

272
00:13:06,030 --> 00:13:08,250
[woman humming]

273
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,670
[metallic clank]

274
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:15,500
[elevator dings]

275
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:19,260
[WOMAN] Huh?

276
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:21,090
[monster growling]

277
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:31,270
[woman whimpers]

278
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:33,610
-[JIN] Hello there, miss.
-[woman gasps]

279
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:35,270
[monster growls]

280
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:37,520
I take it you're able
to see them?

281
00:13:38,110 --> 00:13:39,360
[woman gasps]

282
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,820
[WOMAN] I...

283
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:42,490
Uh...

284
00:13:42,530 --> 00:13:43,700
[Makoto grunts]

285
00:13:44,370 --> 00:13:46,870
-[Makoto growls]
-[Jin shushes]

286
00:13:47,370 --> 00:13:48,700
[JIN] It's our secret.

287
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:52,460
[DERA] To be perfectly honest,

288
00:13:52,500 --> 00:13:54,670
Hana and I
aren't told much, either.

289
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:56,000
[HANA] Why would we be?

290
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:58,800
Our families have lived
down here for generations.

291
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:01,220
The job's a hand-me-down
from our ancestors.

292
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,720
[DERA] I had two orders.

293
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:03,930
Granny Yamaha told me

294
00:14:03,970 --> 00:14:05,760
to keep outsiders
away from the village,

295
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:08,640
and to make sure you twins
didn't fall into enemy hands.

296
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:10,390
She was real insistent
about that one.

297
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:13,980
Otherwise, I supply goods
and relay info.

298
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:16,820
I try and do whatever odd jobs
crop up down here.

299
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,940
I've never actually been
to Higashi.

300
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:20,440
Frankly, it's not my place

301
00:14:20,490 --> 00:14:22,490
to question what
the village elders think.

302
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:26,160
As a Tadera, I follow the rules
that've been passed down to me.

303
00:14:27,370 --> 00:14:28,450
Oh, yeah.

304
00:14:28,490 --> 00:14:31,040
My real name's
Ryu Tadera, by the way.

305
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,870
But you can still call me Dera.

306
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:35,040
In the keep,

307
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,170
Granny seemed terrified

308
00:14:36,210 --> 00:14:38,750
by the idea the assailants
might take me.

309
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:40,750
She even told you
to get me out of there

310
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:42,840
instead of staying
to help fight.

311
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:46,050
So explain it to me.

312
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:47,390
Why are we special?

313
00:14:50,010 --> 00:14:51,730
[RIGHT] They say
it can only happen

314
00:14:51,770 --> 00:14:53,390
on the day of the equinox.

315
00:14:53,430 --> 00:14:55,390
When a twin boy
and girl are born

316
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:57,360
on either side of the sunrise,

317
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:59,820
the world will be torn asunder.

318
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:01,780
To our knowledge,
the last of these twins

319
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:03,900
before you and your sister
were born

320
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,820
some 400 years ago.

321
00:15:06,490 --> 00:15:08,370
Twins dividing night and day

322
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:10,780
were born inside
the same village.

323
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:13,040
In that era,
a war had split the nation

324
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,660
into east and west.

325
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,540
Years prior, another war
had already divided them

326
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,380
into north and south.

327
00:15:20,130 --> 00:15:23,130
Daemon wielders were
manipulating behind the scenes

328
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:24,470
on both occasions.

329
00:15:24,510 --> 00:15:26,010
What are you saying?

330
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,680
That we've both been cursed
to throw the world into chaos?

331
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:31,810
Nay. Those who wish
to abuse your powers

332
00:15:31,850 --> 00:15:33,850
to their own ends
made these problems.

333
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:35,350
Our powers?

334
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,310
But I'm just a normal kid.

335
00:15:37,350 --> 00:15:38,650
For now, yes.

336
00:15:38,690 --> 00:15:39,940
[LEFT] If you would,

337
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:42,940
you have the right
to claim power.

338
00:15:42,980 --> 00:15:45,030
And by the looks
of things back there,

339
00:15:45,070 --> 00:15:46,950
Asa's already claimed it.

340
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:49,370
Indeed.

341
00:15:49,870 --> 00:15:52,240
That was "Break." I'm sure.

342
00:15:53,750 --> 00:15:56,620
[RIGHT] "Break."
It is the ability

343
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,040
to forcibly unravel all things.

344
00:16:00,130 --> 00:16:02,710
Even the strongest of barriers
falls before it.

345
00:16:02,750 --> 00:16:04,500
As easy as cracking an egg.

346
00:16:04,550 --> 00:16:06,840
[LEFT] There's another
half of the pair, "Seal."

347
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,850
The power
to forcibly close all things.

348
00:16:10,890 --> 00:16:12,720
As easy as shutting a door.

349
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:15,810
What happens if the two powers
collide with each other?

350
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,810
It'd be quite the paradox.

351
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:21,230
Have both the powers ever been
claimed at the same time?

352
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:24,520
As far as we are aware,
that is yet to occur.

353
00:16:24,570 --> 00:16:25,610
[DERA] You heard her.

354
00:16:25,650 --> 00:16:27,450
Means no one knows
how that disaster

355
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:28,610
would play out.

356
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:29,950
You think maybe all the rumors

357
00:16:29,990 --> 00:16:31,780
have taken on a life
of their own?

358
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:33,830
Do the villagers
get what's going on?

359
00:16:33,870 --> 00:16:35,410
Seems like a lot.

360
00:16:35,750 --> 00:16:36,910
Good point.

361
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:39,670
I never knew about
the barrier around us, for one.

362
00:16:39,710 --> 00:16:42,380
How did you manage
to get in and out of it, Dera?

363
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:44,590
There's a specific route
you have to take

364
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:46,050
to circumvent it.

365
00:16:46,090 --> 00:16:48,510
Go counterclockwise
around these rocks

366
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:49,720
X amount of times.

367
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,930
Hang a right when you reach
this crossroad.

368
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:55,100
Turn around at the next
and go through the valley.

369
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:58,180
When you hit the big tree,
take a sharp ninety-degree turn.

370
00:16:58,230 --> 00:17:00,140
Pain in the ass to remember.

371
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:04,270
The Tadera clan was trusted
with the route a long time ago,

372
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,280
so I'm able to pass through
the barrier

373
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:07,650
whenever I feel like it.

374
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:10,280
Your own mother's actually
a woman from down the mountain

375
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:12,530
who stumbled upon the path
during a long hike

376
00:17:12,570 --> 00:17:14,450
by coincidence.

377
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:18,660
[DERA] It's not unheard of.

378
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,330
People wander when they're lost.

379
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:22,460
Some happen to wander
the right way.

380
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:25,170
[Nagisa grunts softly]

381
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:28,300
[bird cawing]

382
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:29,460
[NAGISA] Huh?

383
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:31,800
[Nagisa gasps]

384
00:17:32,430 --> 00:17:35,390
[Nagisa pants]

385
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:36,810
[Yuru grunts softly]

386
00:17:40,310 --> 00:17:41,430
[NAGISA] Yuru?

387
00:17:42,140 --> 00:17:44,400
I was born and raised
in a place far away

388
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,650
from the village, you know.

389
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:48,400
And there,
your name means "night."

390
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,150
I would like to return someday.

391
00:17:51,650 --> 00:17:53,950
I'll take you,
your father and sister

392
00:17:53,990 --> 00:17:55,830
and show you where I grew up.

393
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:57,120
[Yuru chuckles softly]

394
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:59,200
[Nagisa chuckles]

395
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:01,080
♪

396
00:18:16,890 --> 00:18:18,510
[birds chirping]

397
00:18:19,850 --> 00:18:21,310
[beeping]

398
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,350
[YURU] Flush when you're done.

399
00:18:25,230 --> 00:18:26,980
Make sure it goes down.

400
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:29,030
Wash your hands.

401
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,740
[Yuru grunts softly]

402
00:18:33,150 --> 00:18:34,360
[YURU] I don't like these things

403
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,990
that roar like tiny dragons
were stuffed in them.

404
00:18:38,030 --> 00:18:40,290
[YURU] Kill the lights
before leaving. Good.

405
00:18:41,870 --> 00:18:43,960
There! I've learned
all the rules

406
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,210
to using the latrine
in this world.

407
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,540
Mm-hm.

408
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:50,420
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

409
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:51,670
[YURU] But still,

410
00:18:52,090 --> 00:18:54,550
can you believe they don't have
to draw any water from a well?

411
00:18:54,590 --> 00:18:56,550
And how come
pushin' those clicky things

412
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:58,550
makes lights appear
out of glass?

413
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,600
Speaking of light,

414
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:02,140
the city looks
positively radiant at night.

415
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,430
And the sheer number
of castles...

416
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:06,270
It's impressive, to be certain.

417
00:19:06,310 --> 00:19:07,810
[RIGHT] How many lords
must they have

418
00:19:07,860 --> 00:19:09,400
to require so many?

419
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:12,570
[YURU] They're not castles.
Apparently, they're homes.

420
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:15,030
Dera said dozens of people
can live in each one,

421
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:16,280
like a vertical town.

422
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,700
[LEFT] The population
of the capital is remarkable.

423
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:21,080
[YURU] No. It's not even
the capital!

424
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:23,410
He said the capital
is called "Tokyo,"

425
00:19:23,450 --> 00:19:25,250
and there are
ten million people in it.

426
00:19:25,290 --> 00:19:26,460
That's preposterous!

427
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:28,460
How do you harvest enough rice
for all of them?

428
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:31,210
There are people here
beyond what the eye can see!

429
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:33,840
Surely, we're in this "Tokyo!"

430
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:36,680
[YURU] Hold on, I know the name.
I'm sure I do.

431
00:19:36,720 --> 00:19:38,470
Hana told it to me.

432
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:40,760
We're in Guntama.

433
00:19:40,810 --> 00:19:43,220
Guntama, yes. I understand.

434
00:19:43,270 --> 00:19:45,310
Well, we should find
no trouble hiding you

435
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:47,980
if these crowds are always
as large as these.

436
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:50,270
The forest is the best place
to hide a tree.

437
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:52,650
And in this forest of men,

438
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:55,990
you're hoping to find the tree
that is your sister. Yes?

439
00:19:58,110 --> 00:19:59,410
Yeah.

440
00:19:59,450 --> 00:20:02,870
Dera and Hana are kind.
They're probably safe.

441
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:07,080
Still, they have direct ties
to my deception.

442
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,410
To that false sister

443
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:10,460
and the villagers
who lied to me.

444
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:12,880
So I can't trust them
completely.

445
00:20:13,590 --> 00:20:16,670
That said, I can't put
full faith in this girl

446
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,930
who calls herself Asa, either.

447
00:20:18,970 --> 00:20:20,470
[children laughing]

448
00:20:20,930 --> 00:20:22,300
[BOY] Can't catch me!

449
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:26,850
Fleeing the village with a child
was no small decision to make.

450
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:28,190
There's a reason.

451
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:30,980
I need to find my parents.

452
00:20:31,310 --> 00:20:32,730
And to do that,

453
00:20:32,770 --> 00:20:35,610
I'll capture this "Asa"
and have her take me.

454
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:38,570
If I may, I'd like your help.

455
00:20:38,610 --> 00:20:40,570
We're looking for someone
in this world

456
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:42,620
where we don't know
our right from our left.

457
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:44,040
Sounds fun!

458
00:20:44,080 --> 00:20:46,540
We haven't had
half as much intrigue in ages!

459
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:49,540
-Let's enjoy!
-You shouldn't be so raucous

460
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:51,920
with matters important
to our master, Right.

461
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,040
He's serious.

462
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:55,960
Then tell me how you're feeling
about it, Left! Do go on.

463
00:20:56,010 --> 00:20:57,260
[LEFT] Hm.

464
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,260
I am not the hunted.

465
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:04,180
I much prefer to be the hunter.

466
00:21:04,220 --> 00:21:06,720
-[Right chuckles]
-[YURU] Mmm-mmm, mm?

467
00:21:06,770 --> 00:21:08,390
Yeah, sounds like a plan.

468
00:21:08,430 --> 00:21:10,310
Good job
lockin' us down a place.

469
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,770
Hey, welcome back.

470
00:21:12,810 --> 00:21:13,860
What's going on?

471
00:21:14,150 --> 00:21:15,900
Hana just gave us the call
we've been waiting for.

472
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,240
Sounds like she found us
a new place to crash.

473
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:21,740
We can finally kiss
living in a car goodbye!

474
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,030
[YURU] Mm...

475
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,200
You said "call."

476
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,740
Is the call coming
from that thing?

477
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:26,990
What is it?

478
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,540
My phone?

479
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:30,120
Um...

480
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:33,170
Where do we even start
with something like this?

481
00:21:33,210 --> 00:21:36,250
It's for sending letters
and voices like a signal fire.

482
00:21:36,290 --> 00:21:38,510
No, that kind of makes it
sound dangerous.

483
00:21:38,550 --> 00:21:41,170
Oh, well, that's about
the gist of it.

484
00:21:41,630 --> 00:21:43,220
Aye, that makes sense.

485
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:45,470
It is for sending out
smoke signals.

486
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:47,510
[YURU] Understood.

487
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:48,560
[Dera chuckles]

488
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:50,930
[DERA]
They'll just believe anything.

489
00:21:50,980 --> 00:21:52,350
The goofs.

490
00:21:55,310 --> 00:21:57,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

491
00:23:28,370 --> 00:23:29,740
Let me introduce you.

492
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:31,830
This is Kotetsu and Jiro!

493
00:23:32,700 --> 00:23:35,540
[YURU] Right! When you leave
the latrine, you...

494
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:36,920
[RIGHT] Kill the lights!

495
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:38,420
[all yelling]
